ient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}+x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6xy-4x+1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6xy-4x+1) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-4y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6xy-4x+1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-4y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6y-4 & 6x \\\\ 6x & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}6y-4 & 6x \\\\ 6x & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}6xy-4x+1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}6y-4 & 6x \\\\ 6x & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}6xy-4x+1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-4y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6(1)-4 & 6(1) \\\\ 6(1) & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}6(1)(1)-4(1)+1 \\\\ 3(1)^{2}-4(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536189 true] [17592186388007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388008 13194139536189 true] [17592186388007 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536189 true] [17592186388007 1041 "field-1" 13194139536189 true] [17592186388007 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388008 13194139536189 true] [17592186388007 1110 #uuid "15013857-3c5c-511c-967a-756d01e848fe" 13194139536189 true] [17592186388008 1034 "6" 13194139536189 true] [17592186388008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536189 true] [1759218