6189 true] [17592186388017 1145 "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}y-3x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}-2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y-3x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}-2x)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{x}^{2}-6xy) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}-6xy)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8y+2 & 8x-6y \\\\ 8x-6y & -6x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}8y+2 & 8x-6y \\\\ 8x-6y & -6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{[\\begin{aligned}8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\begin{aligned}8y+2 & 8x-6y \\\\ 8x-6y & -6x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{[\\begin{aligned}8xy-3{y}^{2}+2x-2 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-6xy\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8(1)+2 & 8(1)-6(1) \\\\ 8(1)-6(1) & -6(1)\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-[\\begin{aligned}8(1)(1)-3(1)^{2}+2(1)-2 \\\\ 4(1)^{2}-6(1)(1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get $({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}-13/32 \\\\ -15/32\\end{aligned}].$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\